<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania refinery shut after running out of crude.</title>
<headline>Lithuania refinery shut after running out of crude.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's Mazheikiai refinery was forced to shut down after running out of crude oil, a refinery official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He told Reuters the shutdown was due to the fact that the company was late signing a supply agreement with Russia, its only source of product. The refinery has been forced to shut down operations previously because of interruptions to its crude oil supply.</p>
<p>The refinery was expecting 350,000 tonnes of crude oil from Russia and operations might resume on Wednesday, the official said.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
